      "deltaSummaryMarkdown": "I inspected the repair delta in `tools/testkit/tests/tools_paths.rs` and `tools/testkit/tests/browser_paths.rs`; no implementation source changed. **F-S01-LEFTOVER-OLD-FOLDERS:** `the_shells_moved_out_of_tooling` now requires `git ls-files -- tooling` to be empty and `tools/android/AndroidManifest.xml` and `tools/ios/project.yml` to be tracked. `the_project_is_tools_browser` requires `git ls-files -- tools-node` to be empty. Both still check the new files and folders exist. I reran the earlier failing scenario myself: with ignored `tooling/ios/GpuxConformance.xcodeproj` and `tools-node/node_modules/x` present, `cargo test -p gpux-testkit --test tools_paths --test browser_paths` passed 10/10 (5+5). I then removed the leftovers, and the working tree is unchanged. **F-S01-ANDROID-MANIFEST-WIRING:** `android_build_links_the_moved_manifest` runs the real `android::build` against a fake pinned SDK with a temporary checkout root. Its runner records every invocation and fails at `aapt2-link`. The test asserts that the argument after `--manifest` equals `android::manifest(root)`, so a hard-coded or stale path in `android.rs` would fail it. The current `check --sprint s01-moves` evidence passes, including `c-testkit-package` at 135 tests, `c-ios-build` and the lane B canary.",
      "reattestedFrom": "b83127ecca2ade4737eb0580ca41589e944598fc6e8ace007c4771da330310d1",
