      "status": "resolved",
      "descriptionMarkdown": "**Expected:** the new groups prove the old locations are gone from the *tracked* tree, and `cargo test -p gpux-testkit` (TOOLS-1) passes in any checkout of the merged branch.\n\n**Observed:** `tools/testkit/tests/tools_paths.rs::the_old_tooling_folder_is_gone` asserts `!repo/tooling.exists()` and `tools/testkit/tests/browser_paths.rs::the_project_is_tools_browser` asserts `!repo/tools-node.exists()` on the working copy. `git mv` leaves git-ignored generated content behind, so every existing checkout keeps `tooling/ios/GpuxConformance.xcodeproj/` (XcodeGen output) and `tools-node/node_modules/` after pulling. The owner's main checkout (`/Users/dinko/work-private/projects/RayX/Gpux`) has exactly these ignored leftovers today (plus `benchmark/target*`, `benchmark/Cargo.lock`, `benchmark/ios/GpuxBench.xcodeproj`). Reproduced in this worktree: creating the ignored `tools-node/node_modules/x` and `tooling/ios/GpuxConformance.xcodeproj` (then removing them) makes `cargo test -p gpux-testkit --test browser_paths` fail at browser_paths.rs:58, and `tools_paths` fails the same way. So the testkit package suite fails on the owner's checkout after merge until the leftovers are deleted by hand.\n\n**Repair:** assert absence of tracked content, not of the folder: e.g. `git ls-files -- tooling tools-node` is empty (or that tracked marker files such as `tooling/testkit/Cargo.toml`, `tooling/ios/project.yml`, `tools-node/package.json` do not exist), and leave whole-folder layout checks to the sprint-2 layout guard over tracked files. Optionally have sprint-2 docs (t05) tell existing checkouts to delete the ignored leftovers in `benchmark/`, `tooling/` and `tools-node/`. Rerun `c-tools-paths`, `c-browser-paths` and `c-testkit-package` afterwards, then rerun them once with the ignored leftovers present.",
